draftB_agent.never_cut_excess:
None. Every never-cut item the draft touches fits within 148 words:
- the two premises with their roles;
- what is not claimed;
- each claim's standing;
- failures, kept as "some passed, some failed".

Not touched, so not counted:
- a deciding hypothesis (the draft states no law);
- an AI label on a reading (no reading; the block itself is marked AI-written);
- an empty axiom report (not cited).

If the coordinator wants the pure core's empty axiom report cited on the screen, its caveat costs about 19 words, giving about 167, 17 over the budget. Naming one failure as it fell, for example "VD1 failed every frozen rule (T5)", would cost about 7 more.
